<title>ITALY: Italy's Palermo sees April CPI at 0.0 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Palermo sees April CPI at 0.0 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>PALERMO, Italy 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Palermo said its April consumer price index stood at 0.0 percent month on month and 1.2 percent year on year.</p>
<p>In March, Palermo's inflation rate was 0.2 percent and 1.8 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Palermo is one of 11 Italian cities publishing inflation data on Monday and Tuesday. The city's CPI weighs 6.80 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to March 1997):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.0    (0.2)    1.2    (1.8)</p>
<p>    Food				  0.0    (0.1)    1.6    (2.9)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.5    (0.4)    2.2    (2.2)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges  -0.3   (-0.1)    0.3    (1.0)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.0    (0.2)    0.0    (0.0)</p>
<p>    Health services		  -0.1    (0.2)    2.8    (3.1)</p>
<p>    Transportation		   -0.1    (0.3)    0.7    (1.6)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture     0.0   (-0.2)    1.3    (1.2)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.0    (0.8)    2.7    (4.3)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.1    (0.1)    0.9    (1.5)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.2    (0.7)    0.4   (-0.2)</p>
